The review has been written to `docs/reviews/physics-constants/phys-const-09-isa-pressure-exponent-precision.md`.

**Summary**: 4 low-severity findings, no action required. HARES' 5.2558761 is correct and traceable to USSA 1976 derivation (deviation ~1.3×10⁻⁸ vs EnergyPlus' 2.4×10⁻⁵). The practical pressure difference peaks at **0.12 Pa** at 3000 m — 400–500× smaller than typical HVAC pressure sensor accuracy. The extra digits are justified by the derivation and do no harm.
